B?lohl?vek considers the Czech national song to be one of the finest anthenes.
He has already said on the radio "Aesko rozhlas" that he has specifically chosen to chant variants to solo, singers with the most representative young voices, which are expressive and popular.
"Since the beginning I have tried to take care that both and even the chorus have a clear diction, that the lyrical is very comprehensible that they are in harmony," he said.
The national anthem will celebrate the 175th anniversary next year.
"Kde domov m?j" was first played in 1834 on the stage of the Stavovskéh divadlo in the original opera Fidlova?ka by Josef Kajet?n Tyl accompanied by the music of Franti?ek ?kroupa.
He acquired the popularity and the people spontaneously made it his own.
The first choke of the song since the foundation of the 1918 Chechropocchia became the natural part of the national anthem.
It has remained one of the seven national symbols even after the birth of the Autonomonomous Czech Republic.
