The MHD Wednesday of Prague will accompany you for the first time also with an electronic tile
Wednesday, October 1, 2008 it will be inscribed in the history of the Prague Transport Company such as the date on which in the metro, tramway and buses will board the first passengers who instead of the paper ticket will have an e-schement tile in their pockets.
At this time they can procure about a hundred thousand people who own their Opencard tile.
Perpassexes can purchase 30- and 90-day-to-annuous (available from January 1, 2009) at the same time recharging their card at the Infopoints and offices of the Transport Company and at the Muzeum Metro Station, M?stek
Separates can already be purchased yesterday on the internet at the page of the Transport Company www.dpp.cz.
More than four hundred customers took advantage of the service before the afternoon.
Those who will begin to use the service via the internet can completely forget the counters at the subway stops where so far they had to make long queues for paper tickets.
Separation can be bought via the internet and on the Opencard reload it on one of the twelve branches of the Municipal Library.
"In these places the passengers have at their disposal a desk with trained personnel that will help those interested in purchasing on the internet and will also register on their card the credit acquired."
In addition to the libraries it will be possible to load the electronic coupons on the Opencards in ATMs and self-service that are installed at metro entrances.
How are these ATMs ?
They’re red, they look like ticket pickliterators, and the passengers have already noticed them at the Roztyly Metro Stops, Budjovick, I.P. Pavlova, Florenc and Vltavsk.
"Now there are five in the whole of the city but by the end of the year there should be 'eighty ones," Opatrn concluded.
The coupon will be inspected instead of by the driver from the ATM.
The ATM service that will start tomorrow is very simple.
It is enough to enter the Opencard card and upon payment of the coupon, it will be charged above.
