“Trueth of the structure of the brain makes it difficult for us to transmit our feeling to animals.
On the one hand the lateral pre-frontal cortex is often connected with human awareness, the associated circuits (this for its direct participation in short memory and executive and control functions).
In man this large area is much more developed than in other primates and it seems that among the other creatures it lacks completely.
At the very least in those aspects of our awareness dependent on the prefrontal cortex, including knowledge, who we are, and the ability to plan and to decide, we thus recognize the basis on the assumption that man differs even from other primates.
Another dramatic peculiarity should present itself in the way of speaking of man: since a large part of life is connected to the language, it is often said that it is linked to consciousness.
In this case the animals could be ruled out.
Although awareness doesn’t depend on the language, it would influence it in such a way that the animal’s awareness, as it is done, certainly differs greatly from the circumstances of our consciousness.
That’s why it’s difficult to find out how consciousness can be seen in other animals.
If it is not possible to measure it as an internal and subjective thing, in analyzing it through one's own experience due to the special hardware, their research will cause us great problems.
The majority of interpretations refer to the content of conscious experience, but apart from that there is another aspect of consciousness to which for science it would be easier for science to have access.
We could analyze the processes of the consciousness of the animals regardless of their contents, and precisely this happens in studies on the short memory of primates , in particular the example of visualization.
Therefore, by this principle, that Christof Koch und Francis Crick follow, passes first to the neural correlates of the consciousness than the causal mechanisms: they could both be identical but not necessarily.
In an interesting way this principle also highlights the pre-frontirial cortex value for the implementation of visualization.
