The OUI general coordinator and member of the Izquierda Unida party, Gaspar Llamazares, has confirmed today that it will be up to the regional federation of the formation to make a decision on the case of the former councillor for Youth and Sport of the Municipality of Seville, Francisco Manuel Silva, who resigned last week following the accusation of clientelism.
"In these cases I'm particularly federalist, and it will be the Andalusian organization to assume its responsibilities," said Llamazares with regard to the re-administration that the party will have to adopt vis-à-vis what has hitherto been an assessor in the Sevigliano council.
