Recurrence drivers of alcoholism will need to install "alcolock".
The Ministry of the Interior requires that drivers with three administrative penalties due to excessive blood alcohol, install in his car the system that prevents driving the vehicle in a state of intoxication or if he does not blow himself into the appropriate device.
The measure was announced last June and is already included in the Annual Report of the Public Prosecutor’s Office of State, according to which it will be a one-kisty pilot project.
The purpose of this project is re-integration of the driver, since this will have to attend a rehabilitation course on the road.
This initiative, in addition to the Prosecutor's Office for Road Safety, will be attended by the General Directorate of Traffic (DGT) and the Fondazione Istituto Tecnologico per il Sicurezza dell'Automobile (FITSA).
According to the statistics, between 30% and 75% of motorists reported more than once for drunk driving then returns to driving the car.
Alcolock would evivite, because it is a system connected to the vehicle that measures the rate of alcohol in the exhaled air and prevents you to start the car if the driver doesn’t blew, or when a concentration of alcohol is detected higher than allowed.
The cost is more than 1000 euros and it would be borne by the penalty.
In this regard, a study carried out in the U.S. in 2007 has shown that vehicles equipped with such devices allow to be reduced by up to 65% of infragments committed during the first year of introduction.
And in Spain it is estimated that it could save the lives of 115 people a year.
The measure is confined to administrative sanctions for two reasons: to curb these behaviors before they become criminal offences.
