In Guilvinac, the "committee of the crisis" will in fact decide on Tuesday the future actions of the movement and the eventual participation in the meeting scheduled at the Ministry of Agriculture and Fisheries in Paris.
But some Breton anglers don’t want to be portrayed by the heads of the National Fishing Committee, who didn’t support the movement.
"The strike will continue" because "the fishermen will not give up" and "they "have no intention of moving to Paris", announced, for example, Liliane Cariou, chairman of the Lorient fishing committee.
Prosecutive fishermen, who do not pay taxes on the diesel, currently pay about 50 cents per liter, but estimate that the yield limit of a boat is reached only with a diesel oil of less than 0.30 euros per liter.
