Excessive liciting psychology: Why Spend More Money?
At auctions, shoppers are inclined to overestimate goods.
Neurologists and economists at the University of New York were able to unravel the neuro-ecoposals of this well-known and seemingly irrational behavior.
According to their study published in the journal Science the men do not want to be left behind in a competition such as the eBay auction, so they are willing to pay even a higher price.
The research tried to trace the nervous pattern of this "game" at the level of the nervous system through experimental rods.
One group of volunteers gambled on the lot, the other group of gamers participated in an auction while with the Functional MRI (fMRI) method they looked at the active areas of the brains of the participating people in the experiment.
Participants could win money in both games, but in the auction game, in which the substantive element is liciting more than the other, the streaked body under the cerebral cortex intensely comes into operation when it loses at the gamble.
In addition to other functions, this brain area plays a role in the "autogratification" mechanism of the nervous system.
Therefore, according to the researchers, the rise in the price is explained by shrugging the vehement reaction of the shrilled body.
In order to uphold their theory, the research group’s economists carried out a financial pursuit investigation.
In this survey, three groups lay against a partner under different conditions.
To the control group they reported the real value of the product in question and they made their bet.
To another group in addition to this they have promised that in the case of winning they will receive another prize of 15 dollars.
On the other hand, the third group would have received $15 prior to the auction, but the members of the group would have lost the money in the event of an auction.
The difference between the two bands consisted in the fact that for one of them the payout was emphasized, while for the other the loss.
Probing the neurologists hypothesis, the members of the group who played "against the loss" were willing to make higher bets of the control or "winning" group.
"These findings are not deductible from any of the previously existing economic theories.
These in fact until now explained the phenomena that can be found at the auctions with the joy of winning and the avoidance of the risk.
“Une methods of neurologic image creation have helped to solve the contradiction between the two theories, so that we have come to a third explanation,” said Andrew Schotter, a professor in the Faculty of Economics at the University of New York.
Hepatitis: When should I turn to the doctor?
Nearly half a billion people in the world are suffering from chronic hepatitis B or C, but chronic hepatic diseases are among the leading causes of death.
In Hungary the number of hepatitis patients amounts to one hundred thousand, of which only 7,000 are cured: the reason is that many patients do not know they are infected.
Hehepatitis is the collective name for contagious hepatic diseases caused by different viruses.
“There are a lot of similarities between the symptoms, typical are hepatitis and jauntaprotinuity, but their pathogens and diseases caused differ from each other.
Hepatitis viruses spread in two main forms depending on the pathtogenic agent: Hepatitis A and E through the alimentary canopy (e.g. water and infected foods), hepatitis B, C, D, and the other viruses with blood and organic fluid (sperm, vaginal discharge, saliva).
It is useful for travelers to vaccinate against virus A and B, there is no vaccine against C.
Hepatitis-again symptoms appear two- to three weeks after consumption of infected foods, accompanied by general malaise, weakness, ab abdominal pain and nausea.
Then yellowish stains are formed on the skin and the white of the eyes, the stools become light and the dark urine, the healing takes place within two to three weeks.
A million people die every year around the world from Hepatitis B, the most serious variant of the disease, which causes liver tumors and cirrhosiatics.
The main reason is, it is estimated that only one out of ten people receive pharmacological treatment.
Hepatitis C can also have very serious consequences: if left untreasure it can cause liver cirrhosis and liver tumours.
Most infected people don’t know they’ve contracted the disease because pathogens subtly destroy liver cells, in many cases the first symptoms appear after 20 to 30 years.
It’s very important the prevention and execution of regular medical analysis.
“This disease is much more frequent than the average in three groups—those who had a blood transliption before 1991—addiaddicts—addiaddicts—and-thre-at-created.
The number of people infected by the chronic hepatitis C virus in the world currently amounts to $200 million.
Since a routine lab examination also reveals the disease is worth contacting the family doctor when noticing any symptoms of unknown origin.
Recognized in time the disease is curable, the virus can be eliminated from the organism, so the infectious power ceases and the formation of tumors can be prevented.
Sept. 30 is World Hepatitis Day, first organized in 2004 around the world by patient associations.
The aim is to draw attention to chronic viral hepatitis, the causes of its development and the early recognition of the disease.
Who Believes in God He Feels Less Pain?
According to the result of a recent investigation the religious faith functions as a kind of analgesic that has rendered the death of the Catholic martyrs more tolerable.
Scientists at the University of Oxford carried out an interesting experiment, looking at the way faith in the god affects the sensation of pain, the British Telegraph said.
As part of the quarrelsome investigation an electroshock was carried out to 12 Catholic believers and as many atheists, while everyone observed a painting depicting the Virgin Mary.
According to the results, Catholic believers were able to refute much of the pain.
Thanks to exploroctive technique of the human brain it was discovered that Catholics were able to activate the part of the brain responsible for pain control.
The test is the first of a series of studies in which in addition to the academics also take part scientists, philosophers and theologians of the University.
The test took place exactly like this: an emitting tool that emits unloads and passes the electroshock has been connected to the left hand of the subject of the experiment.
The researchers asked the participants to concentrate on two paintings, the Virgin Mary painted in the seventeenth-to-celf by Sassoferrato in the 17th century and the Damethem by Leonardo da Vinci painted in the fifteenth-century.
The perpetrators of the examination hoped that the image of the Virgin Mary gave rise to a sort of religious state among the believers, while Leonardo's painting was chosen because it did not differ too much from the other and they considered it a reassuring effect.
Subtomers of the experiment spent half an hour in front of the MRI scanner and in this groping time they received 20 electroshocks in four consecutive series, while observing or the religious-themed painting or the other.
Catholics have reported that the vision of the Virgin Mary made them feel "secure", as if "someone took care" of them and "reassured and were pervaded by peace".
Looking at the religious-themed image they accounted for 12% less pain compared to when they were in front of Leonardo's work ahead of them.
The psychologist Miguel Farias, who himself took part in the test, believes that such a result can be achieved with any high-image effect even for atheists, but it is necessary to find a suitable image.
“We have to look for an image to which they have very positive feelings, such as a mother or a father.”
Anglican Bishop Tom Wright was pleased with the result of research.
"The practice of faith should change, and in many cases it manages to change our personality."
After the excellent results remains only the question of whether the painting of a magina by Leonardo or of another painter of similar caliber is presented to believers, what effect could it have on the control of pain?
Would the vision of a virgin Mary of quality bring better results?
You're What You Say About Yourself
On her tenth-birth-birth-fizday, Google can claim to be in people’s pockets as in the sky above their heads; she knows where they’ve spent their holidays, which clinic they’re attending and what they’re interested in.
But this, according to Eric Schmidt, one of the directors of the company, is still not enough.
On the other hand, what concerns skeptic skeptics who make a comparison with the Orwellian nightmarish, they do not really see the substance of web 2.0.
“Recently Eric Schmidt told the Financial Times that Google’s main purpose is to collect as many personal data from its users and that’s necessary to stick to Google’s original goal that it was: “let’s insert all the information in the world into a system!”
According to the director of Google interviewed the company, after 10 years of revolutionary work, it is still at the beginning to be able to manage all the information.
To the question what will happen in five years Schmidt replied: he’d like him if Google could answer questions like “what do I do tomorrow?” or “what’s the right job for me?”, but the software can’t answer seemingly simple questions because they don’t know enough about users.
