The President George W. Bush spoke on Saturday night with Pelosi, then greeted with joy at the White House the news of the agreement.
“We’re pleased with the progress we’ve achieved tonight, and we really appreciate the two parties’ efforts to stabilise our financial markets and defend the economy,” said Tony Fratto spokeswoman for the White House.
However, the program differs from the Bush administration’s original proposal, which stipulated that $700 billion would all be spent on the purchase of securities with disproportioned receivables behind them.
It will now be possible to spend at most half the sum of $ 700 billion, $250 billion immediately after Monday’s congressional vote, with it the Ministry of the Treasury will buy bonds with disproportioned reliance on the back, the fate of the remaining 100 billion dollars will decide the president.
A special constituency will control the program in which the President of the Federal Reserve also participates.
